"aqueous_phase":"water","doi":"10.1007/s00775-012-0889-9","year":2012,"record_id":"MLDB-004808","detection":"FAAS","method_description":"Lipophilicity of the platinum complexes was quantified as log P (logarithm of the 1-octanol/water partition coefficient). The log P values were determined according to the OECD guideline using a shake-flask method [25], as was previously done with platinum complexes [26–28]. Weighed amounts of platinum compounds were partitioned between an aqueous and a 1-octanol phase. Platinum concentrations in both phases were measured by flameless atomic absorption spectrometry. The partition coefficients were calculated on the basis of these results."}]}